/-!
# The scalar moment threshold for the (19,23) certificate

This file proves the target threshold for the explicit proposed lower moment
sum. It does not assume or prove that the 3,645 widths attain that lower sum;
`Odd437Certificate` proves that separately.

Generated by `scripts/generate-odd-thresholds.py`. With `D = 10^50`,
the first ladder starts at `2431132176156040890913535684 * (D / 10^24)` and the second at
`3628411 * D`; each later entry is the integer square root of the previous entry
times `D`, rounded up in the second ladder. The rounded log endpoints are the
floor, respectively ceiling, at denominator `10^30` of `2^80*(1-D/lo)` and
`2^80*(hi/D-1)`. Here `F = 19^3 * 23^2 = 3628411`. Every entry and the final comparison are checked by
Lean.
-/

